orgen fortryder, ikke noget, Du nu bilder Dig ind\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"During an emotional reunion, Maria asks whether the speaker's apparent change is genuine, enduring, and not something he will regret the next day or has imagined merely because he missed his lover. He answers with an emphatic avowal: “as surely” as he has tended to say too little rather than too much, he loves her.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression contains no clear undertaking; it avows love. A neighbouring statement presents Maria as the person with whom the speaker intends to live for a very long time and ultimately die, but that is separate from the target. Maria's tears and happiness show that she receives the avowal as truthful reassurance, not necessarily as assent to a specifically defined undertaking.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognise the work from the supplied text.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly represents the avowal as sincere, including the narration that Maria understands he is speaking truth. It does not, however, provide precise practical terms for the neighbouring future-oriented commitment or establish any formal relational agreement.\"}"
